    "result_text": "All 69 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS), including the new `Cp57Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change enqueues a welcome notification on successful owner creation, emitting a line on the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and memberId.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n- Reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and logs `Welcome owner id={} memberId={}` on the `NOTIFY` logger. It runs after `save` so the generated id is available, mirroring the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `notifyWelcome` step between `audit` and `respond`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe step sits on the success path only (after all validation/quota/duplicate checks and `save`), so notifications are only emitted for owners actually created. Verified output: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
